    "question": {
      ":question/id": "80919dbb-52a9-543f-9adb-242ef12b7428",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(- 3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(e^{2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,2]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- 3 e^{2 t},\\qquad y=e^{2 t},\\qquad z=- 2 e^{- 2 t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =x\\,\\mathbf{i}+z\\,\\mathbf{j}+y\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(- 3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(e^{2 t}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =- 3 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(e^{2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =- 6 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+4 e^{- 2 t}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- 3 e^{2 t}\\right)\\left(- 6 e^{2 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 e^{- 2 t}\\right)\\left(2 e^{2 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(e^{2 t}\\right)\\left(4 e^{- 2 t}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(18 e^{4 t}\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(4\\right) \\\\ & =18 e^{4 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(18 e^{4 t}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[\\frac{9 e^{4 t}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{9 e^{4 \\left(2\\right)}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(\\frac{9 e^{4 \\left(0\\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{9 e^{8}}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{9}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =- \\frac{9}{2} + \\frac{9 e^{8}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
