    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8b14d0a8-764d-5189-b796-38395ce9fb22",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(\\frac{z}{x}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(\\frac{z}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(- e^{3 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(- 3 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,2]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=- e^{3 t},\\qquad y=e^{t},\\qquad z=- 3 t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{z}{x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{z}{y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(- 3 t\\right)}{\\left(- e^{3 t}\\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\frac{\\left(- 3 t\\right)}{\\left(e^{t}\\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =3 t e^{- 3 t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+- 3 t e^{- t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- e^{3 t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 3 t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =- 3 e^{3 t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+e^{t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+-3\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(3 t e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\left(- 3 e^{3 t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 3 t e^{- t}\\right)\\left(e^{t}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(1\\right)\\left(-3\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 9 t\\right)+\\left(- 3 t\\right)+\\left(-3\\right) \\\\ & =- 12 t - 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(- 12 t - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[- 6 t^{2} - 3 t\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 \\left(2\\right)^{2} - 3 \\left(2\\right)\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(- 6 \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 3 \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(-30\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$",
